# CleanNest — repo hygiene (never commit these)
.env
.env.*
*.local
.DS_Store
node_modules/
*.log
Thumbs.db
.hermes/
.review/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. Never commit these.
#
# Cloudflare Pages runs `npm run build` and publishes the repo root, so every
# one of these is regenerated at deploy time and the committed copy is never
# what gets served. Keeping them tracked meant two things: the working tree
# showed ~80 modified files after every single build, and the committed copies
# silently drifted — before this, all 55 committed HTML files pointed at a
# superseded stylesheet hash while production was serving a newer one.
#
# The build writes only into these paths and touches no source file, so a
# fresh clone plus `npm run build` reproduces the exact tree that deploys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*.html
/blog/*.html
/assets/generated/
/sitemap.xml

# Meta domain verification (18 Sept 2026). Meta fetches this exact URL and
# checks the token inside, so it must be TRACKED and served — it is not build
# output, it is an input. The `/*.html` rule above would otherwise swallow it
# silently: the file copies in, git reports a clean tree, nothing is pushed,
# and Meta sees a 404. The negation must stay AFTER /*.html to take effect.
!/pxawfl5xxh0yig08fro10644ikkd84.html

# Deliberately NOT ignored: assets/catalog.json. The build regenerates it, but
# tests/estimate.test.mjs reads it directly, so a fresh clone needs it present
# to run `npm test` without building first.
